Template: openvox-ca/ca-name
Type: string
Default:
Description: Certificate name for this host:
 openvox-ca issues this host a node certificate and serves its API with it.
 Agents check that name against the server name they are configured with, so
 it should be the fully qualified name they use to reach this host.
 .
 Unless an admin list is already configured (puppet_server in
 /etc/openvox-ca/config.yaml, or a systemd drop-in), the certificate is also
 made a CA administrator, so that this host can sign, revoke and clean
 certificates through the API.
 .
 Leave this empty to let provisioning choose: the certname in puppet.conf if
 there is one, otherwise this host's name. This host's certificate is then
 not made an administrator: it cannot sign, revoke or clean until
 puppet_server in /etc/openvox-ca/config.yaml names it.

Template: openvox-ca/ca-name-invalid
Type: error
Description: Unusable certificate name
 "${name}" cannot be used as a certificate name. A name may contain only
 letters, digits, dots, dashes and underscores, and may not begin with a dash.
 "ca" and "openvox-ca-server" are reserved: the package uses them for aliases.
